#!/usr/bin/env etcs
#IMPORT ACE_ROOT/modules

# The same 3D scene as scene3d.etcs, projected THROUGH the device instead of
# into host pixels.
#
#     ./bin/etcs scripts/scene3d_gpu.etcs
#
# and then, from the prompt while it runs:
#
#     Root> eye.SetDeviceProjection(0)     # back to the CPU, live
#     Root> eye.SetDeviceProjection(1)     # and back again
#     Root> RenderProvider                 # log file  -- just this module
#
# ONE LINE IS THE WHOLE DIFFERENCE from scene3d.etcs, and it is not the toggle:
# it is the Device spawned under the camera. The toggle only asks; what makes
# the ask answerable is that child existing (ontology/Device.h).
#
# WHY A CHILD AND NOT A FLAG. There is always a CPU. Host memory is the floor
# every raster in this system already stands on, so it needs no declaration --
# which makes a device strictly an ADDITION, and in this ontology an addition
# is a child. The capability is then a fact about the entity graph: enumerable
# by the same typed-child walk everything else uses, on the state surface like
# every other origin-affixed tag, and marking the camera's observers when it
# appears or goes. A boolean on the camera would have been a second copy of
# that, settable to a value the graph disagrees with.
#
# It also means "which device" is the same mechanism as "whether": two Devices
# under one camera is two devices available to it, with no new concept.
#
# AND THE FALLBACK IS FREE. Delete the Device child mid-run and the camera
# quietly draws on the host again -- the effective mode is the request AND a
# device still being there, derived at read time rather than stored, so the two
# can never disagree (ontology/Camera.h).
#
# WHAT ACTUALLY CHANGES DOWNSTREAM. Nothing above the sink: the view, the
# flatten, the near clip, the perspective divide, the fan and the depth test
# are arithmetic about a scene and a lens, identical either way. What differs
# is where a surviving run of pixels goes -- written as bytes into the camera's
# buffer, or emitted as one DrawRect through the destination. On a
# VulkanSurface those are device rects, so the frame is produced by the GPU and
# never exists as host pixels at all. That is the same thing
# PolygonDrawable2D has always done one dimension down.

spawn RenderProvider::Instance gpu
gpu.Create()

spawn WindowProvider::Window main
main.Create(1024, 768, 'ETCS 3D scene -- device projection')

main.spawn(RenderProvider::Surface view)
view.Create(@gpu)

spawn RenderProvider::CompositeDrawable2D stage
stage.Create(1024, 768)
stage.SetPosition(0, 0)
stage.SetBackground(0.04, 0.05, 0.08, 1.0)

stage.spawn(RenderProvider::Camera3D eye)
eye.Create(1024, 768)
eye.SetPosition(0, 0)
eye.SetOrder(1)
eye.SetBackground(0.07, 0.09, 0.15, 1.0)
eye.LookAt(0.0, 3.0, -14.0, 0.0, 0.5, 2.0)
eye.SetLens(60.0, 0.1, 400.0)

# ── the capability, and then the ask ─────────────────────────────────────
#
# Spawned under the camera rather than attached from the root, because `attach`
# is a pure lookup and does not re-parent (doc/etcs_specification.md): a
# relation gets INTO the tree by being created there. The Device names the
# Instance by RID and answers for it, so there is one Vulkan device in this
# process, not two -- the child is the capability, not the hardware.
eye.spawn(RenderProvider::Device dev)
dev.Create(@gpu)
eye.SetDeviceProjection(1)

spawn RenderProvider::Scene3D world
world.Create(1.0, 1.0, 1.0)
world.SetVisible(0)
world.SetPosition(0.0, 0.0, 0.0)
world.SetSpeed(7.0)
world.SetDamping(6.0)
world.SetSensitivity(2.0)
world.SetEmissivity(0.5)

run RenderProvider/scripts/scene3d.etcs anchor=world

eye.SetScene(@world)

# ── 2D UI on the camera's frame ──────────────────────────────────────────
#
# Unchanged from the host version, and that is the point worth watching: these
# are children of the camera and know nothing about how their parent's frame is
# produced. In device mode the camera owns no picture for them to be drawn
# into, so they compose onto the destination exactly as the camera's own spans
# do -- same tree, same order, same coordinates.
eye.spawn(RenderProvider::TextLabel hud)
hud.Create(24)
hud.SetText(%f fps -- device projection -- wasd move / mouse look / ctrl+tab)
hud.SetPosition(16, 16)
hud.SetColor(0.6, 1.0, 0.7, 1.0)
hud.SetBackground(0.0, 0.0, 0.0, 0.45)
hud.SetPadding(6)
hud.SetOrder(11)
hud.BindFps(@view)

eye.spawn(RenderProvider::PolygonDrawable2D reticle)
reticle.Create()
reticle.AddPoint(506, 378)
reticle.AddPoint(518, 378)
reticle.AddPoint(518, 390)
reticle.AddPoint(506, 390)
reticle.SetFill(1.0, 1.0, 1.0, 0.55)
reticle.SetOrder(10)

view.Clear(0.02, 0.02, 0.03, 1.0)
view.Compose(@stage)

main.CaptureMouse(1)

detach scene3d_input.etcs window=main scene=world
detach RenderProvider/scripts/render_frames.etcs view=view gpu=gpu
detach scene3d_profile.etcs main=main gpu=gpu view=view
